{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoinduced Co/Ni-cocatalyzed Markovnikov hydroarylation of unactivated alkenes with aryl bromides. This method utilizes protons from a Hantzsch ester as the hydrogen source, avoiding the need for hydrosilanes or oxidants. The reaction proceeds via a Co-III-H species generated from the reduction and protonation of a Co-I intermediate, enabling the construction of C(sp2)-C(sp3) bonds and quaternary carbons with high regioselectivity.",
